# SLACATHON 2026 Backend - Environment Configuration Example
# Copy this file to .env (or export the variables in your shell / systemd / docker)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# REQUIRED: API Keys (comma or space separated)
# These are the only keys that will be accepted via the X-API-Key header.
# Generate strong random keys for real use (e.g. using: openssl rand -hex 16)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
SLACATHON_API_KEYS=key_abc123def456ghi789,another_strong_key_here

# Optional: You can also set them directly:
# export SLACATHON_API_KEYS="key_one key_two key_three"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Other runtime config (currently have reasonable defaults in code)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# MAX_QUERIES_PER_USER=10
# LEADERBOARD_SIZE=15

# The following files are used for persistence (created automatically if missing):
# - user_names.json   (maps API keys to human display names)
# - leaderboard.json  (top scores)

# Note: Never commit real keys. The old hardcoded development keys
# (key_123 etc.) are only used as a last-resort fallback when the
# environment variable is not set, and will log a warning on startup.
